description:
User approved 2026-11-24 for the end of the fz-9x7 epic (relayed by GC).

Rule (user): the runtime never constructs, allocates or computes anything only to report it. An event passes its data through as-is; the receiver copies or computes what it wants.

First case: GcStats.from_space_capacity_bytes is a sum over every from-space block (runtime/src/heap/imp.rs:1609), computed on every collection. Only telemetry.rs:243 reads it, along with blocks_released.

Planned shape:
- collect returns the from-space blocks unreleased;
- RuntimeEvent::Gc carries &[Block];
- end_quantum releases the blocks after observe;
- the handler computes len and the capacity sum only when a log is attached.

Scope also covers auditing every GcStats field and every other RuntimeEvent for the same pattern.

Related: fz-9x7.11.7, a collection writing its statistics into a caller-owned slot instead of returning GcStats by value. Reconcile with it: fields this ticket removes shrink what .11.7 moves.
